TION includes named party's estimate. So include.\n\nLet's include figures for E1-E4, E6. E3 percentages are financial measures? Yes, share of BOM. Include. E5 no figures. E7 no exact figures.\n\nE3 figures:\n- measure \"Memory share of bill of materials\", period \"GB200 vs VR200\", value \"5 to 10 percent on GB200; 25 to 30 percent on VR200\", kind \"estimate\", basis \"Morgan Stanley bill-of-materials analysis\"\n- measure \"GPU share of bill of materials\", period \"GB200 vs VR200\", value \"roughly 63 percent on GB200; 51 percent on VR200\", kind \"estimate\", basis \"Morgan Stanley bill-of-materials analysis\"\nThis is okay.\n\nE4 figures:\n- \"Rubin GPU price per unit at volume\", period \"Vera Rubin generation\", value \"$55,000\", kind \"estimate\", basis \"Morgan Stanley estimate, volume pricing\"\n- \"Vera CPU price per unit at volume\", value \"$5,000\", kind \"estimate\", basis \"Morgan Stanley estimate, volume pricing\"\n\nE6 figures:\n- \"Vera Rubin rack price per unit if hyperscaler self-sources certain memory modules\", period \"Vera Rubin generation\", value \"around $6.7 million\", kind \"estimate\", basis \"conditional on self-sourcing certain memory modules\"\n\nE2 figures:\n- \"Memory content per Vera Rubin rack\", period \"Vera Rubin generation\", value \"about $2 million\", kind \"estimate\", basis \"Morgan Stanley estimate\"\n- \"Memory cost increase vs prior generation\", period \"generation-over-generation\", value \"435%\", kind \"estimate\", basis \"Morgan Stanley estimate\"\n- \"3D NAND storage content per rack\", period \"Vera Rubin generation\", value \"roughly $1 million or more\", kind \"estimate\", basis \"Morgan Stanley estimate; virtually absent from earlier systems\"\nMaybe \"LPDDR5X capacity\" 54 terabytes is not financial; omit. But it's a useful figure? Not financial. The schema says financial measure. Omit.\n\nE1 figures as above.\n\nNeed maybe include \"GB300 NVL72 rack price\" value \"roughly $4 million\" kind estimate. Ye